WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:10.670
Home to 7.2 Billion people planet Earth is
a 5 billion year old ball of Iron, Oxygen,

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:19.579
Silicon, Magnesium, and other trace elements,
hurtling through space at 67,000 mph.

00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:25.530
Earth is a rather incredible place to be,
here's some of the most extreme facts about

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:31.000
the planet you live on.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.710
1.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.100
Earth used to be purple.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.340
From space, land on the Earth's surface appears
mostly green.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.480
But millions of years ago it would have been
purple.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.370
Today plants use a green pigment called chlorophyll
to harness the sun's rays which gives them

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.910
a green appearance.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:59.129
But research shows that chlorophyll hasn't
been around forever, in fact during the days

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:05.590
of early life on Earth plants used to use
a more primitive molecule to harness the suns

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:06.590
rays.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:13.070
It was called Retinal, and it gave off a violet
hue instead of a green one.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:19.799
Meaning all photosynthesising plants on Earth
were, at one point bright purple.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:20.799
2.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:26.180
But the dominant colour on Earth's surface
definitely isn't green.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:31.939
When the first astronauts that went into space
looked back at our planet, they called it

00:01:31.939 --> 00:01:33.509
the "Blue Planet".

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:41.130
That's not surprising when you consider that
Earth's surface is 71% water.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.299
3.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:48.969
With all that water you would think we would
know more about what's down there, but 95%

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:55.369
of Earth's underwater world still remains
unexplored.

00:01:55.369 --> 00:02:01.609
That's a remarkable testament to how astonishingly
vast the oceans actually are.

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:02.609
4.

00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:07.050
Only 3% of water on Earth is fresh water.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.690
The remaining 97% is salted water.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:19.760
And what's more, of the 3% of fresh water,
2% of it is frozen in ice sheets and glaciers.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:27.940
Meaning that less than 1% of water on Earth
is fresh water found in lakes, rivers and

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:28.940
underground.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.940
5.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.530
The Earth's core is as hot as the Sun.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:38.070
The Earth is like an Onion, it is made up
of three separate layers, the core, the mantle

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.810
and the crust.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:47.420
The core is made up of mostly molten iron,
bubbling away at an incredibly toasty 6,100

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:52.580
degrees celcius, making it as hot as the surface
of the Sun.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:03:00.129
Despite this intense heat, the very centre
of the Earth's core remains solid iron, because

00:03:00.129 --> 00:03:05.100
of the immense amount of pressure put upon
the core from the weight of the rest of the

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.100
Earth.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.100
6.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:12.250
There is single mountain range that stretches
around the entire globe.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.050
Known as the mid-ocean ridge system.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:22.470
It's an impressive range of underwater volcanoes
that spans the entirety of Earth's oceans.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:28.319
It was created from volcanic eruptions of
basaltic lava that occurs between the Earth's

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:29.629
tectonic plates.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:37.990
At a monstrous 60,000 kilometres long, the
mid-ocean ridge system is the largest geological

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.030
feature on Earth.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:45.810
The closest contender above ground is the
Andes mountain range in South America, which

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:52.890
is a measly 7,200 kilometres in comparison
to the underwater giant.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:53.910
7.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:04:00.900
Earth is the only planet in our solar system
that isn't named after a mythical God.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.900
8.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:08.079
Earth isn't actually a sphere it's a shape
known as a geoid.

00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:14.000
This simply means that the rounded ball bulges
outwards at the equator.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.510
But what's even more incredible is what causes
Earth to be this shape instead of a perfectly

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.450
formed sphere.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.770
Earth spins on its axis at 1,000 mph.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:34.190
Such a high rotational speed exerts an incredible
amount of centrifugal force upon the equator,

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.970
pushing the earth and water around the equator
outwards slightly.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.880
Giving the Earth somewhat of a spare tire.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:43.880
9.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.050
Space is dirty.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:52.410
Every day our planet is sprinkled with massive
quantities of interstellar fairy dust.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:59.770
100 tons of space dust and various other debris
drifts down into our atmosphere and onto the

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.640
Earth's surface every day.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.570
Most of it comes from other planets and comets.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.570
10.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:12.900
And finally, in the interstellar scope, Earth
is tiny, really tiny.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:20.030
For example, if you compare it to the planet
Jupiter, Earth could fit inside Jupiter 1,321

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.030
times.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:29.770
And if you think that's impressive, nothing
will make you feel more like a microscopic

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:39.530
dot in the vast nothingness of space than
this fact, Earth could fit inside the Sun

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.720
13 million times.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:47.600
But don't get downbeat, Earth is very special
and extremely unique.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:53.590
Earth is the only planet we know of that has
given birth to life.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:06:00.130
It has just the perfect conditions, the perfect
temperature and proximity to the Sun, it has

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.730
water and a magnetic field that protects us
from the Sun's violent radiation, as well

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.860
as many other important factors.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:14.530
The chances of all these coming factors coming
together to create a planet that can sustain

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:22.030
life is this .0000000000000000000001% or 1
in this number 10,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:27.940
So the fact that we're even here to begin
with is a mathematical miracle.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:36.140
And that's what makes Earth so amazing.

